\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces PointProgrammerNet architecture. Red paths carry the three equal-size additive FWP states after historical points have been discarded. The segmentation head reads each state at query coordinate $\bm  {q}$, then concatenates the decoded context, coordinate skip, and category code. The classification head decodes fixed rows and adds a bounded fine--broad residual to the middle-state summary. Neither head reconstructs or pools over a decoded point set.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{5}{PointProgrammerNet architecture. Red paths carry the three equal-size additive FWP states after historical points have been discarded. The segmentation head reads each state at query coordinate $\bm q$, then concatenates the decoded context, coordinate skip, and category code. The classification head decodes fixed rows and adds a bounded fine--broad residual to the middle-state summary. Neither head reconstructs or pools over a decoded point set}{figure.1}{}}
